Z||000001||fierosound||03-11-2001||05:33 PM||||Sorry to burst your bubble - there's no such thing as CHEAP HEADERS for a V6 Fiero.  You also can't have CHEAP and BEST in the same sentence.  The headers by FOCOA are considered the best by many people.  You may want to consider Sprint manifolds from Fiero Store instead.<P>FOCOA headers<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/images/34engine/header.jpg">  <P>Use the SEARCH function to search for "headers" topics<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-11-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||03-11-2001||05:45 PM||||I agree...<BR>  The words CHEAP and BEST don't belong in the same sentence...<BR>I could make you a cheap set of headers, but would they flow or last?<BR>If you need decent, working headers, then you have to pay the price...||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||03-11-2001||06:16 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/Exh_gif/Flowell_right_500_low.jpg"> <P>our headers have shown to provide a significant gain in horsepower and torque, perhaps you may want to consider us, btw - the sprint headers are great, unfortunatley when you get down and do the numbers they do not add that great of an increase due to the fact that they utilize the stock y-pipe. Our headers are each hand made and use nascar approved connecting clamps, you will not find a better deal<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula 18||03-11-2001||10:00 PM||||IMHO.. Headers may look really nice but you can have almost the same HP gains for porting you stock manifols.<P>Run a search there is TONS of info here about this debate and how to's. <P>Brian ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||03-11-2001||10:18 PM||||If you have a friend that does your exhaust work, get some late model Camaro manifolds and use them. They are cast iron, but have larger passages than the Fiero manifolds. The custom exhaust will be a pain in the rear, but I got mine for less than $150. Now, if you are willing to take a chance, if the factory Camaro manifolds can be made to work, then the headers for the same car could also be made to work. Keep in mind, you will not have a Y-pipe any longer so there is a lot more room on the tranny side of the engine. Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||08:53 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6header1.jpg</A> <P>cwestco headers on my/GT Bastards 86 SE. unless your running a larger motor, nitrous or a S/C you'll be dissappointed with their performance.<P><BR>you might want to try thier shorty header... they mave have more backpressure and give you better torque numbers.||||reg||1
